    "provenance": {
      "type": "official-sdk",
      "authority": "aircraft-vendor",
      "access": "vendor-install",
      "supportsActiveMappings": true,
      "name": "iniBuilds A380 1.0.0 normal gear handle behavior",
      "url": "https://docs.flightsimulator.com/msfs2024/html/2_DevMode/Menus/Tools/Behaviours_Debug/Behaviors_Debug.htm",
      "retrievedAt": "2026-10-17",
      "notes": "Loaded vendor behavior export SHA256 5dd0b57e906e9c537c64411264fc39f41100a08d57e36fd0c9ef2b7647276700, AIRLINER_MIP_LG_HANDLE owner 1540. Set 0 invokes INI.GEAR_UP only airborne; Set 1 invokes INI.GEAR_DOWN. The native input event retains this aircraft-owned ground interlock. FlightFabric also requires fresh SIM ON GROUND=false before UP and confirms GEAR HANDLE POSITION, not completed gear travel. Generic surface fallback remains disabled. On 2026-10-17, A380-800 RR Basic in MSFS 2024 passed production recognized-text DOWN no-op and UP ground inhibition with no writes. Airborne UP, repeat UP no-op, DOWN and repeat DOWN no-op passed with two native writes; the three standard gear-position readings reached 0 then 100 percent. Handle selection confirmed in about one second, independently of the approximately 21-second retraction and 35-second extension. Final handle and standard gear positions were DOWN. Current package/simulator build numbers and other variants were not established. See docs/INIBUILDS-A380-ONBOARDING.md."
    }
  },
