    "provenance": {
      "type": "official-sdk",
      "authority": "aircraft-vendor",
      "access": "public",
      "supportsActiveMappings": true,
      "name": "TFDi MD-11 requested surface and FCP event contract",
      "url": "https://docs.tfdidesign.com/md11/integration-guide/events",
      "retrievedAt": "2026-10-17",
      "notes": "Vendor CEVENT contract and variables, cross-checked on 2026-10-17 with TFDi Design MD-11 PW4462 (Low Poly Cabin) in MSFS 2024. Autobrake 82212 increases and 82211 decreases MD11_CTR_AUTOBRAKE_SW: T.O.=0, OFF=1, MIN=2, MED=3, MAX=4. All selections and restoration passed through the production command service; repeat MED sent no writes. Flap 77831 increases and 77830 decreases MD11_FLAP_RNG: UP=0, 0/EXT=20, 28=70, 35=82, 50=100. Dial-a-Flap 10, 15 and displayed 25 yielded 38, 46.91 and 64.73 with dial animation 0, 33 and 99. The variable detent is decoded in a bounded 38-65 interval; 65 is the endpoint inferred from the observed linear span, not a separately observed selector value. A moving lever can traverse the takeoff interval; confirmation requires a fresh MD11_FLAP_LATCH=0 sample at least as recent as the handle sample. The final production run selected 0/EXT, TAKEOFF, 28, 35, 50 and restored TAKEOFF, with independently settled surface angles. UP was observed as the initial no-op baseline; its transition after the settled-readback correction remains untested. Spoiler 77828 increases, 77853 decreases MD11_SPDBRK_RNG: RET=0, 1/3=17.5, 2/3=25, FULL=32.5; ground overtravel is excluded. MD11_SPDBRK_HANDLE 0 is disarmed and 1 armed; standard SPOILERS ARMED did not follow disarming. Left button 77829 arm/disarm and same-state no-op passed. Production FULL from armed first confirmed disarm, then stepped to FULL; all intermediate choices and RET restoration passed. FCP pairs FMS SPD 86088/86089, NAV 86090/86091, APPR LAND 86092/86093, AUTOFLIGHT 86094/86095, PROF 86096/86097 press/release once and acknowledge delivery without claiming engagement; live FMA acceptance remains pending. The vendor forward-panel guide defines AUTOFLIGHT as ATS on ground and AP/ATS airborne; no independent AP/ATS toggle or ATS-state enum is inferred. All actions share the CEVENT lock and fresh power guard. These are selector checks, not airborne or automatic-braking qualification. See docs/MD11-CONTROL-VALIDATION.md for exact evidence and pending acceptance."
    }
  },
